A step that ran is edited: the database ran the step as it was, so the
ledger no longer says what happened to it, and a database that had not run
it would get another history. Refused, saying both texts and what to do;
nothing changes. Comments between steps are not part of them, so a
comment changed or added is no edit (deploy 2).

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'Pea Soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN slug TEXT;
UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(name);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;

== ledger
-- Slugs, for URLs.
ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN slug TEXT;
UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(name); -- spaces stay: see below

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN slug TEXT;
UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-'));

== plan
-- after 1
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's steps 1 to 2
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN slug TEXT;
  step 2
    UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(name);
-- after 2
-- after 3

== error
-- after 3
ledger.sql's step 2 is not what the database ran. It ran:
  UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(name);
ledger.sql says:
  UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-'));
A step that ran stays as it is: put it back, and add a step after it. (A database that ran a draft of the step, a dev one: put back the copy made before it, in `<database>.before-ledger/`.)

== query
SELECT id, slug FROM dish

== rows
1 | pea soup
